Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||06-05-2001||01:37 PM||||The indiglow is kind of a fluke.. I have a friend who has connections at 3M, the stuff usually costs $108 for a tiny sheet (not enough to do a fiero dash) with all the associated hardware..<P>As for designs , I can do pretty much anything, keep in mind there not backlite. The cheapest way to do it is get non backlight gauges from an 84 (not sure on 85) I'm using thatsetup until I get the indiglow done<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
